00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.920
And now, back to the show.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.050
The Boy puts power front and center.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.400
Since we're dealing with a world

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.290
where some people can leap buildings,

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.820
or obliterate an innocent woman,

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.140
in a single bound.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.400
But just as importantly,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.930
a whole lot of people can't.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.430
And all of this sounds in line

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.290
with Michel Foucault's analysis

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.150
of how power functions in society.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.610
One form of power he
identifies, sovereign power,

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.140
describes the right of those

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.360
at the top to give and take life,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.440
or, to put it more simply,

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.520
the right to kill.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.430
We see a lot of this in
modern political philosophy.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.690
In this view of power,

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.550
there's a small contingent at the top

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.010
who can take all of us out at will

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.840
and then we're just down at the bottom,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.460
hoping that they don't.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.580
And ever since A-Train plowed
through Huey's girlfriend

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.770
and Homelander took out an entire plane

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.730
to protect the company,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.830
The Boys has been exploring how dangerous

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.020
this type of sovereign power really is

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.430
and how those who wield it

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.200
rarely face consequences.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.940
This is why, at least initially,

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.370
it seems like we're
watching a valiant quest

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.510
by Butcher and the boys

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.980
to level the playing field

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.510
by overthrowing the supes

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.550
and the force of their sovereign power.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.860
But as we go further down
the Vought rabbit hole,

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.710
it becomes clear that the
power problem isn't limited

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:20.940
to the wielding of power

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.860
by a powerful sovereign,

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:24.090
a la what Hobbes

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.160
and the modern political
philosophers talked about.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.930
Rather, power is more defined

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.227
by what Foucault describes as,

00:03:29.227 --> 00:03:32.887
"Rules according to which the
true and false are separate

00:03:32.887 --> 00:03:34.477
"and specific effects of power

00:03:34.477 --> 00:03:36.037
"which are attached to the true.

00:03:36.037 --> 00:03:38.437
"A battle about the status of truth

00:03:38.437 --> 00:03:41.280
"and the economic and
political role it plays."

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.750
In this way, power is something

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.310
that's sort of everywhere,

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:47.040
and enacted more than it's possessed.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.230
The boys are on a
mission to prevent anyone

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.720
from wielding that type
of power ever again.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.970
But as we go further down
the Vought rabbit hole,

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.000
it becomes clear that the
power problem isn't limited

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.250
to A-Train and co, it's everywhere.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.180
Along with Starlight,

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.070
Huey has been the closest thing

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.690
the show has to a moral compass.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:04.590
We sympathize with him

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.150
because he's been victimized

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:07.920
by multiple members of The Seven,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.870
and he's way more compassionate

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.850
than most of the show's alpha males.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.710
Plus, he's just sort of adorable

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.720
and wears really great T-shirts,

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.250
but he still lives in a world

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.380
where value is measured in power.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.670
And the A-Train action figures

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:21.690
in his bedroom show us

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.850
that he grew up admiring supes.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.170
He desires power

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.060
but has spent most of his life without it,

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.410
and the tension this creates

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.380
soon starts bubbling
up in unpleasant ways,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.870
some of which involve intravenous drug use

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.983
and green puke.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.630
Now, Huey's frustration seems

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.950
to come from a good place.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.930
He's watched his loved ones being harmed

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:43.950
without being able to help

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.930
so he wishes he was stronger,

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.460
but there's something else going on

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.490
and it manifests in his
insecurity about dating a supe.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.080
The struggle to open a jar threatens

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.400
his sense of manhood,

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.230
even when they're safe at home.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.130
On some level,

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.630
Huey feels entitled to be

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.310
more powerful than Starlight

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.840
simply because he's a man.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.550
His sense of worth is derived

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.380
from how powerful he feels,

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.060
specifically relative to his

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.770
incredibly powerful girlfriend.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.540
- I thought that you
didn't care about that.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.570
I mean, on our first date,

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.993
you said that it didn't bother you.

00:05:13.993 --> 00:05:14.826
- I know.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:21.303
But it does.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.313
Sometimes.

00:05:25.313 --> 00:05:27.510
- [Michael] But this
isn't just a Huey problem.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.550
Society prioritizes power,

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.900
which we see in the throngs

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.880
of sad sacks obsessed with Homelander,

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.940
all getting off on his
all-encompassing power.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.560
This seemingly harmless

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.170
but toxic dude-ness is
exemplified by Todd,

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.360
a classic nice guy type.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.830
He's a glasses-wearing,

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.300
flannel shirt-clad teacher,

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.280
and caring stepfather and husband.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.570
But we learn that underneath

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.610
the nice guy exterior is

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.560
a dark obsession with Homelander

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.230
and his most toxic and violent beliefs.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.000
- 'Cause he's America's greatest hero

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.070
who saves thousands of people.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:00.780
He's standing up to the crooks,

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:03.360
the corporations, and the legacy media.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.530
Hey, you friend me on Facebook,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.889
I'll send you some stuff.

00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:06.722
- And I mean...

00:06:06.722 --> 00:06:08.031
Okay, let's just say it right now.

00:06:08.031 --> 00:06:09.930
In particular, in season three,

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:10.950
they're doing a Trump thing.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.930
I mean, you saw the
taco bowl scene, right?

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.970
- Seriously, we have the best taco bowls

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.380
right here in the building.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.477
Should make you feel right at home, pal.

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:20.040
(speaking foreign language)

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.600
- Trump literally did that.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.917
And the whole, "I could
shoot someone on Fifth Avenue

00:06:23.917 --> 00:06:25.230
"and nothing would happen" thing.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.400
- Where I could stand in the middle

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.080
of Fifth Avenue and shoot somebody,

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.670
and I wouldn't lose any voters, okay?

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:31.020
- [Michael] Well, that happens too.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.580
And it goes just about as well

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.190
as old Don Sr. predicted.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.023
- Yeah!

00:06:35.023 --> 00:06:37.347
(crowd applauding)

00:06:37.347 --> 00:06:39.510
- [Michael] And while
Huey doesn't have Todd's

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.360
dark obsession with
Homelander's fascist worldview,

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.100
he does fall into the same trap

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.720
of being the nice guy

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.970
who fetishizes the power of others.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:50.610
The introduction of Temp V allows Huey

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.620
to experience the physical power

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.360
that A-Train and Homelander have used

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.470
to ruin his life,

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.780
and the transformation is stunning.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:58.920
Formerly peaceful,

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.210
Huey starts killing people

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.420
with his bare hands

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.753
while naked.

00:07:05.211 --> 00:07:06.320
- Oh (beep), I'm sorry.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.670
- If I was murdered by
a fully clothed man,

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.350
I would feel a sense of honor.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.790
If I was murdered by a naked person,

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.870
I would feel shame.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.040
I'd feel nothing 'cause I'd be dead

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.960
but assuming that the afterlife exists

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.760
and consciousness transcends
into the afterlife,

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.593
I would feel shame.

00:07:18.593 --> 00:07:19.860
We can better understand

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:20.790
what's going on here

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.140
with another type of power

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.280
that Foucault talks about:

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.180
Biopower.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:25.087
Foucault describes it as

00:07:25.087 --> 00:07:28.327
"An explosion of numerous
and diverse techniques

00:07:28.327 --> 00:07:30.787
"for achieving the subjugation of bodies

00:07:30.787 --> 00:07:32.460
"and the control of populations."

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.230
Biopower is another mechanism

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.480
by which societies can control

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:37.639
who lives or dies

00:07:37.639 --> 00:07:39.720
while ensuring the health

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.010
of a stable workforce.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.990
This can look like, I don't know,

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.450
like governments deciding when life begins

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.850
and what bodies containing
life are allowed

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:48.870
to do with them.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.090
Sorry, I know that was a
super hypothetical example.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:52.440
I'll do a better one next time.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.730
And in the world of The Boys,

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:57.030
both Compound V and Temp
V represent advances

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.830
in a type of biopower

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.050
by which certain humans literally have

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:02.790
more biological power,

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.740
which they can decide to use

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:06.300
to hurt or to help people.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.220
So Huey's pacifism, empathy,

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.320
and loyalty to Starlight all dwindle

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.630
as soon as he is jacked up on that V.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.670
It's almost as if he was just using

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:16.200
these virtues as crutches that,

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.200
once empowered, he no longer found useful.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.880
- I thought the drugs had
(beep) you up, Huey, but

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:25.703
this is you.

00:08:29.626 --> 00:08:30.780
This is all you.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:31.830
- [Michael] Luckily, by
the end of the season,

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.720
we learned that Huey isn't, in fact,

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.610
a total power hungry piece of (beep).

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:38.167
- Literally, every neuron
in your brain is screaming

00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:39.000
"I told you so,"

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:39.833
so why don't you just say it

00:08:39.833 --> 00:08:41.550
before your head explodes?
- Oh my God!

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:43.560
I (beep) told you so.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.900
- But not everyone comes back to the light

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.280
after tasting some power.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.980
And power dynamics aren't
exclusive to the men.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.120
The show's female characters

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.530
also find themselves forced

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.861
to compromise their values

00:08:53.861 --> 00:08:56.940
if they want to enjoy agency or authority.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.300
Take the shameless
corporate climber, Ashley.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:03.000
- I accept your nomination as CEO

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.013
of Vought International.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.160
You know, my mother used to say,

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.380
before she died of cancer when I was 17--

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.810
- Okay, Ashley, that's enough.

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:14.160
Let's not bring the room down.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:14.993
- Apologies, sir.

00:09:14.993 --> 00:09:16.830
- [Michael] Having worked
her way to the top at Vought,

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:18.210
she gets a front row seat

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:21.270
to Homelander's brutal corporate culture.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.280
But being humiliated every day

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.590
by those above her doesn't inspire Ashley

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:26.730
to change the system

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.560
or challenge its legitimacy,

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:31.170
though it does lead to her
ripping out her own hair.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.990
Instead, she just soaks up all their abuse

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:36.840
and unleashes it on those
not as strong as her.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.130
- The next report you're gonna be doing is

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.900
inside my (beep) asshole...

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.010
- [Michael] Putting women like Ashley

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.570
in positions of power seems like

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:45.270
it should challenge the
patriarchal culture at Vought.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.980
That, at least, is the theory

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.990
of the "Lean In" brand of feminism,

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:50.580
sometimes called "corporate feminism,"

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:51.990
which has been championed by the likes

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:54.600
of former Facebook COO, Sheryl Sandberg.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.280
The thinking goes that women climbing

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.830
the ranks can change
things from the inside,

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:01.200
tipping the balance and
fundamentally altering

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.610
sexist power structures.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:04.020
Unlike most third wave feminists,

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:06.210
corporate feminism doesn't view capitalism

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.130
as part and parcel with gender inequality.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:09.783
Rather, it argues that equality comes

00:10:09.783 --> 00:10:11.970
when capitalism diversifies.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:14.130
It's sort like saying that

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.410
the planet of Alderaan would still exist

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.910
if the Death Star were pink.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:19.620
In reality, and much like Ashley,

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.870
Sandberg's been accused
of wielding her power

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:23.880
in less than savory ways.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.310
She reportedly yelled at
and intimidated employees

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.270
when they tried to speak up

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.460
about Facebook's role in Russia's campaign

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.290
to influence the 2016 election,

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.270
and she reportedly
failed to act decisively

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.250
to stop the prolific dissemination

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:37.410
of right wing extremism, racism,

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:38.910
and misogyny on the platform.

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:39.960
But to be clear,

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.910
to the best of our knowledge,

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.890
Sandberg has never been complicit

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:45.840
in any murders or kidnapping

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:46.990
that we're aware of.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:49.200
On the show, Ashley embraces

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.270
a type of "Lean In" feminism,

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.340
even as she's actively harming

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.390
the women around her.

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:56.610
She ends up mimicking
Homelander's example.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:59.370
- Is your idiot brain
getting (beep) by stupid?

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:01.950
- Is your idiot brain
getting (beep) by stupid?

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.230
- [Michael] Several other
female characters do the same.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.340
Before Homelander went

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:07.260
all "Raiders of the Lost Ark" on her,

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:08.730
Madelyn Stillwell was able to hold

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.040
some sway over the superpowered man-baby,

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.770
but only by indulging
his edible fantasies.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.483
Our boy likes to drink that milk.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:18.360
Also, in this season,

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.310
he milks a cow to suck its teat

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:21.990
'cause his edible fantasies transition

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:22.980
to farm animals,

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.918
but we don't kink-shame at Wisecrack.

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:26.751
- Nope.

00:11:26.751 --> 00:11:28.080
- And Madelyn had no qualms

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.280
with all types of murder

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.780
and intimidation and bribery,

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:32.040
as long as it helped her climb

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.180
the corporate ranks.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.070
Even superpowered women are forced

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:37.080
to occupy a specific version

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.030
of the "strong woman" archetype.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.050
When she joins The Seven,

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.930
Starlight's costume is
immediately reinvented

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.280
to make it more revealing.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.020
You know, for the fellas.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.099
She can be strong,

00:11:47.099 --> 00:11:49.560
just as long as she's also sexy.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.000
And while Vought goes out of its way

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.320
to highlight how empowered

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:53.520
its female heroes are

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.650
with their "Girls get it done" slogan...

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.090
- Girls get it done.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.200
- [Michael] They always ensure that

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.630
their vision of a powerful
woman does nothing

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:03.030
to challenge the authority
of the patriarchy.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:06.300
- Wow, I'm so honored to
be with you guys tonight

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:09.330
to celebrate my dear friend

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.640
and mentor, Homelander.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.140
- [Michael] Even when
they seem to be acting

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.510
outside the bounds of
conventional gender roles,

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.554
they're still just playing with power.

00:12:17.554 --> 00:12:18.742
- (indistinct)

00:12:18.742 --> 00:12:20.370
- [Michael] Stormfront's
whole identity was based

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:22.980
around rejecting the
traditional feminine qualities

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:24.474
of someone like Starlight.

00:12:24.474 --> 00:12:28.230
- (beep) this world for
confusing nice with good.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:30.120
Be a bitch if you want, be whatever,

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.700
just drop the mask once in a while.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:35.130
- [Michael] But this "not
like other girls" branding was

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:35.970
only skin deep

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.400
because her casual Nazism still comes

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.454
in a conventionally feminine package.

00:12:40.454 --> 00:12:41.287
- Yay.

00:12:41.287 --> 00:12:42.720
- It's a lot like the
"cool girl" archetype

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:43.553
from "Gone Girl,"

00:12:43.553 --> 00:12:45.210
where her subversions are acceptable

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:48.630
in so much as they don't
challenge gender roles themselves.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:49.560
Also, at the end of the day,

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:53.160
she still ends up being
Homelander's half-dead HJ machine.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.156
- When you lead an army
of Aryan ubermensch

00:12:56.156 --> 00:12:58.017
to their victory.
- What?

00:12:58.017 --> 00:12:59.970
- The key thing here is that no matter

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:01.800
how high any of them climb,

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.300
the moment they stop playing along

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.140
with the powers that be,

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.477
the moment they improperly
express empathy,

00:13:07.477 --> 00:13:10.140
they can be easily thrown under the bus,

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.120
or tossed into a secret prison,

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.490
or just taken out all together.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:17.730
This makes any kind of
solidarity almost impossible.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.250
Vought takes full advantage
of the women's disunity

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.980
when it wants to get rid of Queen Maeve.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:24.450
While positioning her as a symbol

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:27.240
of empowered queer womanhood
was great for marketing,

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.130
the moment she starts to speak out,

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.210
she vanishes.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:33.330
And when Starlight appeals
to Ashley's humanity

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.290
to try and find her,

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.630
we see a split second of empathy,

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:37.463
and then...

00:13:37.463 --> 00:13:38.767
- I am CEO.

00:13:38.767 --> 00:13:40.770
Next time, make a (beep) appointment.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.540
- From soft boys like Huey

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.400
to superwomen like Starlight,

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.870
what the third season of the show

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.090
really underlines is how difficult it is

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.520
to actually take a stand against

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.470
the types of power that philosophers

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.580
like Foucault talk about.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.380
When describing his theory of biopower,

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:57.487
he says that "If genocide is indeed

00:13:57.487 --> 00:13:58.957
"the dream of modern power,

00:13:58.957 --> 00:14:01.177
"this is not because of the recent return

00:14:01.177 --> 00:14:02.647
"to the ancient right to kill.

00:14:02.647 --> 00:14:04.297
"It is because power is situated

00:14:04.297 --> 00:14:06.187
"and exercised at the level of life,

00:14:06.187 --> 00:14:07.417
"the species, the race,

00:14:07.417 --> 00:14:10.140
"and the large scale
phenomena of the population."

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.360
Which means that modern power uses

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:15.180
as much force as necessary to maintain

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.460
the structure of a governable society.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.360
- Nobody wants innocent people
to get hurt, of course not.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:24.783
But sadly,

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.483
well, the bad guys,

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:30.783
they don't think like us.

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:36.450
And so, sometimes,

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.340
well, these things just happen.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.720
- Now, we can better understand

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:41.250
what's going on here by visiting

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:42.930
another pair of French thinkers,

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.940
Gilles Deleuze and Félix Guattari,

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.590
who we would assume Frenchie has

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:49.860
definitely read while in
a philosophical K-hole.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:52.074
- You know, Jean-Paul Sartre said,

00:14:52.074 --> 00:14:55.680
"Marriage stifles our
essential male urges."

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:57.390
- Their work understands modern power

00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:58.860
via the lens of capitalism,

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:00.870
and how human desire is structured

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.760
and then used by capitalism.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.250
This allows them to analyze
how capitalism seems

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.140
to be able to suck everything up

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:08.270
into its own orbit,

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:11.550
infinitely increasing its
own power and control.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:12.487
According to Deleuze,

00:15:12.487 --> 00:15:14.407
"Everything is rational in capitalism

00:15:14.407 --> 00:15:17.287
"except capital or capitalism itself.

00:15:17.287 --> 00:15:19.597
"The stock market is certainly rational.

00:15:19.597 --> 00:15:21.247
"One can understand it, study it,

00:15:21.247 --> 00:15:22.867
"the capitalists know how to use it,

00:15:22.867 --> 00:15:24.847
"and yet it is completely delirious.

00:15:24.847 --> 00:15:25.680
"It's mad.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.517
"It is in the sense that we say

00:15:27.517 --> 00:15:30.127
"the rational is always the rationality

00:15:30.127 --> 00:15:31.560
"of an irrational."

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:32.490
This is a key tension of

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.448
how power operates under capitalism.

00:15:34.448 --> 00:15:36.540
It makes logical sense,

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.170
i.e we can understand how markets

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:41.850
and profits work in mathematical terms,

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:43.440
but it's also totally batshit

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.400
when we realize

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:47.880
how these logical systems
affect society and human life.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.500
It makes logical sense

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.510
that student loan debt comes

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.220
with compounding interest,

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.720
but it makes absolutely no sense

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.450
that a kindergarten teacher
can rack up six figures

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.470
in growing debt.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:15:59.820
And we see this in Vought,

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:01.740
a publicly traded corporation

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.540
that makes logical decisions based on

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:04.650
how it affects the market

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:05.820
and their profitability,

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:06.870
even when the reality of

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:09.720
those decisions involves
murdering innocent humans,

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.340
or experimenting on children,

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.040
and empowering a superpowered psychopath.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.410
It's what makes Homelander
such a perfect metaphor

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.750
for this kind of capitalist-fueled power.

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:19.950
He's literally bulletproof,

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.480
able to shrug off any attack,

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.380
any criticism,

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.120
any call for accountability,

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:25.530
because at the end of the day,

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:26.940
he still has all the power.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:29.130
And as long as his
power doesn't contradict

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.300
the logic of capital,

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.685
everything is fine.

00:16:31.685 --> 00:16:33.690
And that's what people who really want

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:35.010
to change things are up against.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.780
A powerful structure that can

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:38.730
logically justify taking you out

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.110
if you're (beep) with their profits,

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:42.693
and that has the biopower
to kill you with ease.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.390
Take the three characters

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:46.890
who seemed like they were leading

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:48.900
the charge against Vought and Homelander:

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.810
Starlight, Billy Butcher,
and Victoria Neuman.

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:53.970
They're each taking different approaches

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:54.803
to changing things,

00:16:54.803 --> 00:16:57.390
with Butcher aiming for
a violent insurrection,

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.460
Neuman hoping to bring
about political change

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:00.900
via the democratic process,

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:03.780
and Starlight trying to
fix Vought from the inside.

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:05.640
Now, initially, it seems like

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.170
they're all making a difference:

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.150
Butcher is effectively tracking down

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:11.130
dangerous superheroes while reining in

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.690
his most violent impulses;

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:15.060
Neuman is leading the
Bureau of Superhero Affairs

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.590
to try and keep those with powers

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.330
within the bounds of the law;

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.460
and Starlight has been made co-captain

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.293
of the The Seven,

00:17:21.293 --> 00:17:23.010
seemingly putting her on equal footing

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:23.843
with Homelander.

00:17:23.843 --> 00:17:26.340
It looks like real change is coming,

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.920
but that idea is quickly set on fire,

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:29.820
snapped in half,

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:31.260
and stomped into the dirt,

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.010
and then it gets its head blown up.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.300
Neuman is revealed to
be in Vought's pocket.

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.940
This makes sense as the
corporation is so powerful

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:40.110
that it can own everyone

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:42.330
on both sides of the political divide,

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.040
propping up progressive politicians

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.060
to maintain the impression

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.230
of a functioning democracy

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:48.060
without risking Vought's own authority.

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:50.280
Oh, and Neuman is, of course, also a supe

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:51.360
who can blow people's heads up.

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:54.030
But hey, at least this is just a TV show.

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:56.220
It's not like corporate
interest would ever have

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:57.660
a direct relationship

00:17:57.660 --> 00:18:00.930
with seemingly progressive
politicians that...

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.700
That allowed them to ensure

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:03.990
that they stayed in power

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:05.250
while pacifying the masses

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:07.230
into thinking that politicians
were fighting for them,

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.090
'cause that'd be crazy, right?

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:11.640
Like, if politicians took money

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.410
from the oil industry,

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:14.670
the weapons industry,

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:15.750
the tech industry,

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:16.583
and then they were like,

00:18:16.583 --> 00:18:17.416
"Oh no, but we care.

00:18:17.416 --> 00:18:18.900
"We care about you," you know?

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:20.910
That's TV stuff, okay?

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.320
Grow up if you think
that's how the world works,

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:23.220
that's TV.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.450
It's not how the world works.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.070
For Deleuze and Guattari,

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.780
none of this fundamentally contradicts

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:28.710
how capital works

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.920
because ideology doesn't really matter,

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:33.000
only power does.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.627
Deleuze says in an interview that,

00:18:34.627 --> 00:18:36.907
"ideology has no importance whatsoever.

00:18:36.907 --> 00:18:38.497
"What matters is not ideology,

00:18:38.497 --> 00:18:41.017
"not even the
economic-ideological distinction

00:18:41.017 --> 00:18:41.850
"or opposition,

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.597
"but the organization of power.

00:18:43.597 --> 00:18:45.307
"Because organization of power,

00:18:45.307 --> 00:18:47.737
"that is the manner in which desire is

00:18:47.737 --> 00:18:49.237
"already in the economic,

00:18:49.237 --> 00:18:51.667
"in which libido invests the economic,

00:18:51.667 --> 00:18:52.777
"haunts the economic

00:18:52.777 --> 00:18:55.500
"and nourishes political
forms of repression."

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.390
Okay, this means that underneath

00:18:57.390 --> 00:19:00.630
a social performance of
ideology and politics,

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.100
like what we see from Neuman,

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.947
is really just a raw desire for power.

00:19:03.947 --> 00:19:07.170
- You've 193 million Instagram followers.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.210
Lend me your influence
and I'll lend you mine.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.783
I can protect you from Homelander,

00:19:10.783 --> 00:19:13.590
you'll finally be team captain for real.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.450
And in return, you'll
help me goose my numbers.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:18.030
- [Michael] This isn't
just about one politician

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.320
secretly being corrupt,

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.730
but a system where power is

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:22.500
so concentrated into the hands

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:23.850
of corporations like Vought

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.530
that no one can even enter the game

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:26.580
without their say-so.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:27.810
Huey might have thought that

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.920
he and Neuman were making

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:31.200
all the right chess moves
to take Vought down,

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.300
but it turns out Vought
owned the whole board

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:34.133
from the beginning

00:19:34.133 --> 00:19:35.580
and Neuman was playing along

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:37.890
because she gets that it's about power

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.120
and not ideology.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:40.410
The same goes for Starlight.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:42.270
Going from a simple country girl

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:43.950
to the head of the executive table,

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.750
she's exactly the sort of success story

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.640
that "Lean In" feminism craves;

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:50.550
Living proof that talented
and committed women can smash

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:51.510
through the glass ceiling

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:52.620
and rise to the top.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.090
Of course, it's quickly revealed

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:55.770
that Vought is still underpinned

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:57.720
by the same values it always was,

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:59.460
namely that they'll say and do

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:01.440
whatever makes their stock price go up.

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:03.870
Feminism is useful if it's profitable

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:04.980
and helps them sell merch,

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:05.820
and that's about it.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.200
- We always seem primed

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:10.217
to celebrate individual advancements,

00:20:10.217 --> 00:20:12.720
individual advancements of black people,

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.370
people of color, women,

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.680
without taking into consideration

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:20.100
that diversity by itself may simply mean

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:24.900
that previously marginalized
individuals have been recruited

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:29.880
to guarantee a more efficient operation

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:32.340
of oppressive systems.

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:34.170
- [Michael] On the back
of numerous scandals,

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.570
it is briefly beneficial to Vought

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:38.340
to put Starlight front and center

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:40.170
to make them look progressive.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.450
Again, they are using
the power of the media

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.790
to create a regime of truth

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:46.500
that helps maintain their position.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.300
But when Homelander tears up the ratings

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.150
with a maniacal rant about
his own innate superiority,

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:54.150
fascism comes right back into fashion.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:56.040
- I am done apologizing,

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:59.070
I am done being persecuted
for my strengths.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:02.040
You people should be thanking Christ

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.930
that I am who and what I am,

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:06.240
because you need me!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.653
You need me to save you!

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:09.743
You do.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.590
I am the only one who possibly can.

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.150
- And none of this
would've shocked Deleuze,

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:19.867
who said that "Fascism too,

00:21:19.867 --> 00:21:21.637
"one must say that it has assumed

00:21:21.637 --> 00:21:22.837
"the social desires,

00:21:22.837 --> 00:21:25.687
"including the desires
of repression and death.

00:21:25.687 --> 00:21:27.607
"People got hard-ons for Hitler,

00:21:27.607 --> 00:21:29.610
"for the beautiful fascist machine."

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:31.620
Though, now it's not hard-ons for Hitler,

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.030
but hard-ons for Homelander.

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:34.980
And kids, if you thought
philosophy was boring,

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.300
that's a famous French philosopher

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:37.357
who wrote the line,

00:21:37.357 --> 00:21:39.630
"People got hard-ons for Hitler."

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.490
So major in philosophy,

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:42.990
the one major where you can write a paper

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:45.150
that says the phrase "hard-ons for Hitler"

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:47.670
and not get sent to the counseling center.

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:50.520
The overarching message of
The Boys' third season is

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:52.828
that the capitalist
power structure can adapt

00:21:52.828 --> 00:21:54.690
to just about anything.

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:57.420
In most cases, it can
even absorb it outright

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:59.250
and find a way to make money off of it.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.690
The sick genius of capitalism,

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:02.580
according to Deleuze and Guattari,

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:04.230
is that since it's fundamentally

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:06.660
about the logic of power and desire,

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.664
and not ethics or ideologies,

00:22:08.664 --> 00:22:11.850
it can suck up anything into its orbit

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:14.550
as long as it can help increase profits.

00:22:14.550 --> 00:22:17.130
Whether it's A-Train's cynical attempt

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:18.660
to use the Black Lives Matter movement

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:20.340
to propel himself back into relevancy,

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:22.710
or the way Vought turns on a dime

00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:25.350
from forcing Maeve to
cover up her sexuality

00:22:25.350 --> 00:22:28.110
to using her to rainbow-wash
the company's image,

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:30.480
even the things which
were specifically created

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:33.033
to curtail their power can be sucked up

00:22:33.033 --> 00:22:35.610
into the big machine and spat back out

00:22:35.610 --> 00:22:36.960
as consumer products.

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:39.780
Starlight realizes this
when Neuman offers her

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:41.280
the latest in a long line

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:44.340
of "ends justify the
means" type propositions.

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:45.870
She's sick of being drawn

00:22:45.870 --> 00:22:47.010
into a rigged game

00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:49.380
and vows to fight from
the outside instead.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.930
Like one of Deleuze's
favorite literary characters,

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:53.700
Melville's "Bartleby, the Scrivener,"

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:54.780
rather than playing along,

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:56.070
Starlight simply says...

00:22:56.070 --> 00:22:57.240
- [Bartleby] I would prefer not to.

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:58.500
- [Michael] And rejects the system.

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:01.410
She also rejects a more
sovereign view of power

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:03.060
when she uses her Instagram Live

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:05.010
to wield power through knowledge

00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:06.510
and media influence.

00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:08.550
She realizes it's entirely possible

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:10.080
that our French friends were right,

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:11.760
that there is no real outside

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:13.080
and no way to challenge a system

00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:15.780
as deeply ingrained as
the one Vought represents,

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.240
but she's sure as hell gonna try.

00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:20.100
- I'm (beep) done.

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:21.550
I'm not doing it anymore.

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:23.130
- You're not gonna be doing anything

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:25.270
if Homelander kills you.
- Yeah, maybe.

00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:26.880
But then, I'll know I'm not working

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:28.800
with a (beep) nut job.

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:31.740
- Of course, whether she'll
be successful is unclear.

00:23:31.740 --> 00:23:35.190
We already know that incremental
solutions just won't work,

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:36.990
that the whole system is broken

00:23:36.990 --> 00:23:38.970
and needs to be completely rebuilt.

00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:41.010
So long as their lives are defined

00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:42.360
by a desire for power,

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:44.130
they'll only be safe once they have it.

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:45.870
And that's the lesson which everyone

00:23:45.870 --> 00:23:48.090
from Huey to Starlight has been beaten

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:48.990
over the head with

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:50.220
throughout the third season.

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:51.390
And while our friends don't

00:23:51.390 --> 00:23:53.040
magically dismantle the economic

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:54.630
and psychic hold of capitalism

00:23:54.630 --> 00:23:55.740
by season's end,

00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:57.630
we do see some rejections

00:23:57.630 --> 00:24:00.240
of the illogical logic of the system.

00:24:00.240 --> 00:24:02.850
Huey realizes how utterly effed up

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:04.950
his search for power in the Temp V was.

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:07.200
And by reflecting on his
father's love for him,

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:09.720
he realizes that actual strength comes

00:24:09.720 --> 00:24:11.280
from taking care of those we love.

00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:12.113
- You know what?

00:24:12.113 --> 00:24:14.043
Dad was there,

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:18.270
taking care of me during
the worst days of his life,

00:24:18.270 --> 00:24:19.590
just trying to keep the lights on

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:22.920
and a roof above our heads.

00:24:22.920 --> 00:24:25.350
- [Michael] This enables
him to throw away the Temp V

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:27.420
and use his not-decaying brain

00:24:27.420 --> 00:24:29.940
to very literally empower Starlight

00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:30.930
to fight fascism.

00:24:30.930 --> 00:24:31.770
And in doing so,

00:24:31.770 --> 00:24:33.810
this shows that Huey is rejecting

00:24:33.810 --> 00:24:36.000
a sort of old school
sovereign view of power

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.530
and enacting a sort of power

00:24:37.530 --> 00:24:39.330
that he has some control over.

00:24:39.330 --> 00:24:42.300
And we see Maeve seemingly
sacrifice her life

00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:43.290
to protect others.

00:24:43.290 --> 00:24:46.530
But none of these virtuous
or just acts take place

00:24:46.530 --> 00:24:50.070
within the system of Vought's
superhero-industrial complex.

00:24:50.070 --> 00:24:51.420
It's not enough to just get

00:24:51.420 --> 00:24:53.760
some of the right people
further up the pyramid.

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:55.320
They won't have any more effect on it

00:24:55.320 --> 00:24:57.270
than the people sitting
next to Homelander.

00:24:57.270 --> 00:24:58.800
It's about pulling the blocks out

00:24:58.800 --> 00:24:59.880
from the very bottom

00:24:59.880 --> 00:25:01.110
and watching it collapse

00:25:01.110 --> 00:25:02.910
so that we can build something new.

00:25:02.910 --> 00:25:04.290
But as we see in Homelander's

00:25:04.290 --> 00:25:06.060
once good natured son, Ryan,

00:25:06.060 --> 00:25:08.250
some people can't help but be attracted

00:25:08.250 --> 00:25:10.650
to the power promised by the system.

00:25:10.650 --> 00:25:12.150
In its exploration of power,

00:25:12.150 --> 00:25:14.220
both at the biological level of supes

00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:15.840
who can dominate the rest of humanity

00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:17.910
and at the level of a larger system

00:25:17.910 --> 00:25:20.460
which runs on the cold logic of capital,

00:25:20.460 --> 00:25:22.800
The Boys seems to be pointing to the way

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:25.170
in which our own world
isn't all that different.

00:25:25.170 --> 00:25:27.030
Sure, we don't have magical juice

00:25:27.030 --> 00:25:27.990
that we can shoot up

00:25:27.990 --> 00:25:29.400
to help us teleport in the buff,

00:25:29.400 --> 00:25:31.590
or superhumans who can laser-decapitate

00:25:31.590 --> 00:25:32.820
a protestor with impunity,

00:25:32.820 --> 00:25:35.250
but we do have corporations working

00:25:35.250 --> 00:25:36.270
alongside the government

00:25:36.270 --> 00:25:38.310
to profit off weapons and power,

00:25:38.310 --> 00:25:40.170
social and political figures tapping

00:25:40.170 --> 00:25:41.640
into populist anger,

00:25:41.640 --> 00:25:44.160
folks from across the
identity spectrum climbing

00:25:44.160 --> 00:25:45.630
the corporate ladder and crushing

00:25:45.630 --> 00:25:47.070
the folks below them on the way up,

00:25:47.070 --> 00:25:49.950
and politicians who are
maybe more into good PR...

00:25:49.950 --> 00:25:53.280
- That's why I proposed and the House,

00:25:53.280 --> 00:25:55.080
Nancy put it in the plan,

00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:59.130
to immediately provide
$10,000 in debt relief

00:25:59.130 --> 00:26:00.570
as stimulus right now.

00:26:00.570 --> 00:26:02.610
- Than they are actually doing the stuff

00:26:02.610 --> 00:26:04.500
they promised to do when we elected them.

00:26:04.500 --> 00:26:05.850
And much like the show itself,

00:26:05.850 --> 00:26:07.560
we're left wondering if those of us

00:26:07.560 --> 00:26:09.090
without any type of superpower,

00:26:09.090 --> 00:26:11.430
whether that be strength,
money, or influence,

00:26:11.430 --> 00:26:14.040
are left to get, symbolically at least,

00:26:14.040 --> 00:26:15.783
run over by those in power.

00:26:17.550 --> 00:26:19.200
But what do you guys think?

00:26:19.200 --> 00:26:21.656
Is this sort of imbalance
just a fact of life

00:26:21.656 --> 00:26:24.240
or can we ever hope to change things?

00:26:24.240 --> 00:26:26.130
Let us know what you
think in the comments.

00:26:26.130 --> 00:26:28.050
Big thanks to all our
patrons for your support.

00:26:28.050 --> 00:26:29.550
Please, don't forget to check out

00:26:29.550 --> 00:26:30.660
our new Patriot features,

00:26:30.660 --> 00:26:31.590
if you haven't already.

